# The brand kit's text files are LF only, in every checkout. The kit is copied
# byte for byte into journey/public/brand/ and printer/print-server/public/brand/
# (scripts/family-assets.mjs), and Git for Windows checks text out as CRLF by
# default (the release workflow builds the installer on a Windows runner), which
# would ship CRLF copies. The fonts are binary and never converted.
# (printer/scripts/test-brand-kit.cjs refuses any CR outright.)
shared/brand/** text=auto eol=lf
shared/brand/**/*.svg text eol=lf
shared/brand/**/*.css text eol=lf
shared/brand/**/*.json text eol=lf
shared/brand/**/*.md text eol=lf
shared/brand/**/*.txt text eol=lf
shared/brand/**/*.ttf binary
shared/brand/**/*.woff2 binary
